Z||000000||Bill Bailey||11-19-2001||03:01 PM||||1987 GT 2.8.  REPLACE COOLING FAN, REPLACE COOLING SENSOR, REPLACE COOLING FAN SWITCH. WHEN YOU TURN SWITCH KEY ON THE COOLING FAN RUNS ALL THE TIME WHERE CAR IS COLD OR HOT.  THANKS FOR THE HELP.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pyric||11-19-2001||03:08 PM||||Are you getting any computer codes?  You can check without a code reader.  (the Haynes manual will tell you how).  <P>You may have a wire grounding itself somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||11-19-2001||05:46 PM||||Bill...assuming no one wired the fan to constantly run, I'll bet the relay is stuck.  It is on the front wall in the drivers side headlight bay.  With the headlight up you can reach in and remove it.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-19-2001||08:02 PM||||First, make sure the AC controls are OFF if it's got AC.<P>It's not the relay... with a stuck relay the fan never shuts off even with key off. (Fan main power is thru a fusible link direct to the battery.)<P>This fan does shut off with the ignition so... It's either wired to run full time or the control circuit is damaged or the switch on the block is bad.<P>start with unpluging the switch on the block.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
